From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] phy: starfive: fix JH7110 D-PHY lane 1 N resistor

The resistance fields for data lanes 1 through 3 share SYSCFG(12),
where the first field is L1N in bits 4:0.  Reusing the L0N mask from
SYSCFG(8) overlaps the L3N field instead.  The combined register write
therefore leaves L1N at zero and changes L3N from 0x10 to 0x18.

Define the L1N field at its documented location and use it for the
SYSCFG(12) write.  The PineTab-V panel uses all four D-PHY data lanes.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: André Machado <machaddr@falanet.org>
---
 drivers/phy/starfive/phy-jh7110-dphy-tx.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/starfive/phy-jh7110-dphy-tx.c b/drivers/phy/starfive/phy-jh7110-dphy-tx.c
index 9ce08c24e034..0ce39cb89f29 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/starfive/phy-jh7110-dphy-tx.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/starfive/phy-jh7110-dphy-tx.c
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #define STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L0N_HSTX_RES			GENMASK(23, 19)
 #define STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L0P_HSTX_RES			GENMASK(28, 24)
 
+#define STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L1N_HSTX_RES			GENMASK(4, 0)
 #define STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L1P_HSTX_RES			GENMASK(9, 5)
 #define STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L2N_HSTX_RES			GENMASK(14, 10)
 #define STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L2P_HSTX_RES			GENMASK(19, 15)
@@ -260,7 +261,7 @@ static int stf_dphy_configure(struct phy *phy, union phy_configure_opts *opts)
 	       FIELD_PREP(STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L0P_HSTX_RES, 0x10),
 	       dphy->topsys + STF_DPHY_APBIFSAIF_SYSCFG(8));
 
-	writel(FIELD_PREP(STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L0N_HSTX_RES, 0x10) |
+	writel(FIELD_PREP(STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L1N_HSTX_RES, 0x10) |
 	       FIELD_PREP(STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L2N_HSTX_RES, 0x10) |
 	       FIELD_PREP(STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L3N_HSTX_RES, 0x10) |
 	       FIELD_PREP(STF_DPHY_RG_CDTX_L1P_HSTX_RES, 0x10) |
